k about what we're putting in  now um the most vulnerable 8 million  households will get 1200 pounds um  everyone will get 400 pounds off their  bill  that really sort of helps with about 50  of this additional increase with the  energy price guide going up that's been  announced between october and december i  need to begin to think about what  happens in january and then in the rest  of next year you should begin to think  surely you've already been thinking  about it of course what i what i meant  is is  we have to deliver four people tell me  what it looks like  so  there's nothing off the table we're  looking at all the options  everything from the chief executive of  scottish power talking about um you know  help where uh uh you know we need to to  maybe  create a some sort of a a fund for  companies to be able to continue uh to  help uh their customers all the way  through to making sure that we target  the help to both households and small  and medium-sized businesses and probably  some larger businesses because my one of  my concerns  is  the scarring effect on the economy if  perfectly viable businesses in  hospitality and  leisure in high-energy use businesses  would actually suffer or  no longer exist because of putin's  use of energy as a as a weapon you said  that you were looking at two separate  plans depending on who was prime  minister how did they differ  well no what we  i think our responsibility is to make  sure we look at the pledges being made  by the different candidates um so uh liz  truss uh has pledged to have a  moratorium on the green levees um do you  support that that would that it  certainly is something that i think will  help uh everyone it's about 150 pounds  of additional help so we've worked up  those options i said general taxation  then wouldn't you well there is uh  hedwig  well not necessarily because actually we  have some headroom at the moment  certainly if you look at uh on the  capital side of the balance sheet we've  g